# Aesthetic Interactive Web Map & External Media Assets Plan

## Context
The goal is to upgrade the Abuja NGO Web Portal's map from a static SVG graphic to an aesthetic, high-performance interactive vector map using only 100% free open-source services (OpenFreeMap + MapLibre GL JS with zero API keys and zero rate limits), completely delete all local media files from `public/media/`, and transition all imagery and video streams across the entire platform to verified external media assets hosted on high-availability CDNs (Unsplash and Cloudinary).

The portal must maintain strict adherence to the Warm Afro-Modernism design system, preserve 100% pass rates across all Bun unit tests, Playwright multi-viewport browser journeys, Impeccable UI/UX technical audits (20/20 score), and Vercel deployment pre-flight checks.

---

## Approach

### 1. Interactive Vector Map Architecture (OpenFreeMap + MapLibre GL JS)
Replace the custom SVG drawing with a modern interactive vector map powered by **MapLibre GL JS** and **OpenFreeMap**'s Positron basemap (`https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron`), which is completely free, open-source, requires no API keys or tokens, and is delivered via Cloudflare's global edge network.

- **Dependency Addition**:
  - Add `maplibre-gl` to `dependencies` in `package.json`.
- **New Component `src/components/map/FCTInteractiveMap.tsx`** (Client Component):
  - Renders a responsive WebGL vector map container bounded to the Federal Capital Territory (`maxBounds: [[6.60, 8.15], [7.90, 9.60]]`, initial center `[7.25, 8.95]`, zoom `8.8`, pitch `15`).
  - Style URL: `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron` (palette matches `#FAF8F5`, `#111113`, `#E5DFD5`).
  - Navigation controls: `maplibregl.NavigationControl` positioned top-right (zoom, compass bearing, pitch).
  - Style switch pill control (top-left): Allows toggling between `Positron` (warm minimal light default), `Liberty` (detailed topography and roads), and `Bright`.
  - GeoJSON Layer Integration:
    - Defines a `GeoJSON.FeatureCollection` representing the 6 Area Councils (`amac`, `bwari`, `gwagwalada`, `kuje`, `kwali`, `abaji`) with real polygonal boundary approximations across the FCT.
    - Adds vector source `fct-councils` and polygon fill layer:
      * Base fill: `rgba(184, 93, 54, 0.12)` (warm terracotta tint).
      * Hover state: `rgba(184, 93, 54, 0.38)`.
      * Selected state: `rgba(168, 82, 44, 0.55)` with inner border glow.
    - Adds line layer `fct-councils-borders` with `#B85D36` stroke (width 2px).
  - Centroid HTML Markers:
    - Adds interactive DOM markers at the exact headquarters coordinates of each council:
      * Bwari: `[7.3756, 9.2789]`
      * AMAC: `[7.4951, 9.0579]`
      * Gwagwalada: `[7.0864, 8.9482]`
      * Kuje: `[7.2345, 8.8789]`
      * Kwali: `[7.0142, 8.8719]`
      * Abaji: `[6.9428, 8.4739]`
    - Each marker renders an accessible HTML button carrying:
      * `id={`council-path-${council.id}`}` and `id={`council-marker-${council.id}`}`
      * `role="button"`
      * `aria-label={`${council.name}. Headquarters: ${council.headquarters}. ${projectCount} active projects.`}`
      * Terracotta / savannah indicator badge with pulse dot and project counter.
      * Click listener triggering `onSelectCouncil(council.id)` and `map.flyTo({ center: [lng, lat], zoom: 10.2, speed: 1.2 })`.
  - Quick Filter Chip Bar (retained at top):
    - Buttons for "All 6 Councils Overview", "AMAC", "Bwari", "Gwagwalada", "Kuje", "Kwali", "Abaji" with `w-full max-w-full min-w-0 overflow-x-auto` to prevent viewport overflow.
    - Clicking a chip highlights the council, triggers `flyTo`, and opens the detail drawer.
  - Telemetry HUD pill (bottom-left): Displays active council, headquarters, terrain, and coordinates.
  - SSR & Hydration Guard:
    - Uses `useEffect` and `useRef` ensuring zero SSR window conflicts.
    - Includes a lightweight fallback parchment skeleton loader while WebGL context initializes.
- **Update `src/components/map/FCTMapCoordinator.tsx`**:
  - Replace `<FCTMapSVG>` with `<FCTInteractiveMap councils={councils} selectedCouncilId={selectedCouncilId} onSelectCouncil={handleSelectCouncil} />`.
  - Retain `CouncilDetailDrawer` integration so clicking any council smoothly slides in the field operations drawer.
  - Delete `src/components/map/FCTMapSVG.tsx`.

