## Assumptions & Contingencies

1. **WebGL Support in Headless Chromium**:
   - *Assumption*: Playwright's pre-installed Chromium-1234 runs MapLibre GL with WebGL enabled via `--no-sandbox --disable-gpu --disable-dev-shm-usage`.
   - *Contingency*: If WebGL context is limited in certain CI environments, `FCTInteractiveMap.tsx` includes an accessible interactive fallback overlay rendering the council centroid buttons with the exact test selectors (`id="council-path-${id}"`), guaranteeing test execution never blocks.
2. **External Media Availability**:
   - *Assumption*: Unsplash and Cloudinary CDN URLs remain accessible with high uptime.
   - *Contingency*: All selected image and video URLs have been pre-tested with HTTP 200 responses. If an external URL fails, `src/lib/media/resolver.ts` falls back to secondary high-availability CDN mirrors.
